ple names: authors list (<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Category:CS1_maint:_multiple_names:_authors_list\" title=\"Category:CS1 maint: multiple names: authors list\">link</a>)</span></span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite_note-13\"><span><b><a href=\"#cite_ref-13\">^</a></b></span> <span>As can be verified using <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Euler_characteristic\" title=\"Euler characteristic\">Euler's polyhedron formula</a></span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite_note-14\"><span><b><a href=\"#cite_ref-14\">^</a></b></span> <span><cite id=\"CITEREFTegmark\">Tegmark, Max. <a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://space.mit.edu/home/tegmark/icosahedron.html\">\"Welcome to the icosahedron home page\"</a>. <i>space.mit.edu</i>.</cite><span title=\"ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=unknown&amp;rft.jtitle=space.mit.edu&amp;rft.atitle=Welcome+to+the+icosahedron+home+page&amp;rft.aulast=Tegmark&amp;rft.aufirst=Max&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fspace.mit.edu%2Fhome%2Ftegmark%2Ficosahedron.html&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AHEALPix\"></span></span>\n</li>\n</ol></div>\n\n<ul><li><a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://sourceforge.net/projects/healpix/\">Official implementation</a> with many languages support (C, C++, Fortran90, IDL, Java and Python) for resolutions up to 0.4 mas (<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Milliarcsecond#Symbols_and_abbreviations\" title=\"Milliarcsecond\">milliarcsecond</a>)</li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"http://home.fnal.gov/~kuropat/HEALPIX/PixTools.html\">Java port</a> of original Fortran code by Nikolay Kuropatkin, supporting resolutions up to 0.3 arcsec</li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://code.google.com/p/healpix-rangeset/\">Java port</a> optimized to use RangeSet, very good for high resolutions</li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://github.com/healpy/healpy/\">healpy</a>: Python wrapper</li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://github.com/astropy/astropy-healpix\">astropy-healpix</a>: BSD-licensed HEALPix for Astropy</li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://github.com/substack/healpix.cxx\">healpix.cxx</a>: c++ code to transform healpix coordinates</li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://github.com/substack/healpix\">JavaScript port</a>: convert between lonlat and HEALPix coordinates in JavaScript</li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://github.com/michitaro/healpix\">Typescript healpix</a>: An implementation of HEALPix in JavaScript / TypeScript</li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://github.com/ziotom78/Healpix.jl\">Healpix.jl</a>: Healpix library written in Julia</li></ul>\n\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nParsed by mw‐web.eqiad.main‐58fdc9498f‐65z8c\nCached time: 20260413141520\nCache expiry: 2592000\nCache expiry source: Module:Citation/CS1 (os.date(%Y))\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [vary‐revision‐sha1, prevent‐selective‐update, show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.336 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.422 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 1088/1000000\nRevision size: 11121/2097152 bytes\nPost‐expand include size: 118368/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 981/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 12/100\nExpensive parser function count: 1/500\nUnstrip recursion depth: 1/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 60624/5000000 bytes\nLua time usage: 0.218/10.000 seconds\nLua memory usage: 5407878/52428800 bytes\nNumber of Wikibase entities loaded: 0/500\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%  352.588 1 -total\n 49.66%  175.112 1 Template:Reflist\n 30.43%  107.306 5 Template:Cite_journal\n 30.26%  106.698 1 Template:Map_projections\n 29.59%  104.340 1 Template:Navbox_with_collapsible_groups\n 17.93% 63.228 1 Template:Short_description\n 10.16% 35.821 2 Template:Pagetype 8.62% 30.394 8 Template:Navbox 6.57% 23.164 5 Template:Cite_web 5.04% 17.759 3 Template:Main_other\n-->\n\n<!-- Render ID 3400df3d-3743-11f1-a77e-43469d7775dd -->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key enwiki: